# Infrastructure code, which does not belong in the application image.
#
# These entries are load-bearing rather than tidiness: the Dockerfile ends with
# `COPY . .`, and terraform state contains generated credentials in plain text.
# Without these lines that state is uploaded in the build context and baked into
# a layer readable by anyone who can pull the image. Excluding .terraform/ also
# keeps the context small, since it holds the provider plugins.
terraform/
k8s/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform/
